{%- doc -%}
  AJ Ships Free — a free-shipping line on a product card.

  WHY THIS IS NOT A BADGE. The card's badge slot holds exactly one thing, and
  that thing is the size of the discount. On a store whose whole promise is a
  bargain, the saving is what stops the scroll; a second badge in the same
  corner either displaces it or crowds it, and "Ships free" loses that contest
  every time against "40% off". So this sits with the PRICE instead, which is
  also where it is most useful — free shipping is arithmetic, not a hook, and
  the shopper doing the sum is looking at the number.

  IT READS FROM THE MEASUREMENT, NOT FROM THE VENDOR. `ship.cost` is a real
  `draftOrderCalculate` quote for this exact product, so a zero here means
  Shopify offered a free rate on this product rather than that its supplier is
  usually free. The vendor shape is a good predictor and not a guarantee — Fuse
  Audio ships six of seven products free and charges $12 on a heavy radio — and
  a claim on a grid of cards is exactly where a shape-level guess would go
  wrong at scale.

  Absent means absent. A product the weekly sweep has not reached yet renders
  nothing rather than being assumed either way.

  THE COST OF DOING THIS AT ALL, stated so it is a choice and not an oversight:
  279 of 1,472 published products ship free, so this marks 19% of cards and the
  other 81% implicitly read as "shipping extra". That is true, and it moves the
  discovery of it from checkout — where it causes abandonment — to browsing,
  where it informs a choice. It is the same trade as naming the supplier on the
  product page.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product
  assign cost = product.metafields.ship.cost.value

  assign show = false
  if cost != blank and cost == 0
    assign show = true
  endif

  # Redundant inside the collection that is DEFINED by this fact — every card
  # would carry it, which makes it decoration rather than information. The
  # collection's own description already says it once, properly.
  if collection.handle == 'ships-free'
    assign show = false
  endif
-%}

{{ 'aj-ships-free.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- if show -%}
  <p class="aj-card-free" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {{ block.settings.label | default: 'Ships free' }}
  </p>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ Ships Free",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Marks cards whose product was measured at $0 shipping. Renders nothing on products that cost something to ship, and nothing on products the shipping agent has not measured yet. Hidden inside the Ships Free collection, where it would be on every card."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label",
      "label": "Label",
      "default": "Ships free",
      "info": "Shipping is charged per maker, so keep this about THIS item — 'Free shipping on your order' would not be true once a second maker is in the cart."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "AJ Ships Free",
      "category": "Product"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
